<%# M13 maker–checker notice (design card ⑦): what happened, why this person got it, what to do (task U.1).
    Dates through bare l(...) → "Mon dd, yyyy" (EmailDateLocalization). %>
<% noun = @record.is_a?(CapitalDistribution) ? "distribution" : "call" %>
<p>Dear <%= @user.full_name %>,</p>

<p><strong><%= @message %></strong></p>

<% if @record %>
  <%# E39 — what is waiting: the record, its fund, its amount and date, and who prepared it %>
  <ul>
    <li><%= noun.capitalize %>: <%= @record %></li>
    <li>Fund: <%= @record.fund.name %></li>
    <% if @record.is_a?(CapitalCall) %>
      <li>Call amount: <%= money_to_currency(@record.call_amount, {}) %></li>
      <li>Due date: <%= l(@record.due_date) if @record.due_date %></li>
    <% else %>
      <li>Income: <%= money_to_currency(@record.income, {}) %></li>
      <li>Distribution date: <%= l(@record.distribution_date) if @record.distribution_date %></li>
    <% end %>
    <li>Prepared by: <%= @record.preparers.map(&:full_name).to_sentence.presence || "not recorded" %></li>
  </ul>
<% end %>

<% case @kind %>
<% when "approval_request" %>
  <p><strong>Why you got this:</strong> <%= @actor&.full_name || "A colleague" %> asked for this <%= noun %> to be approved.
  Your firm requires a second person to approve capital calls and distributions (maker–checker), so the people who
  prepared it can't approve it themselves. You have the Approver role and access to this fund, and you did not
  prepare it.</p>
  <p><strong>What to do:</strong> open the <%= noun %>, check its figures and click <strong>Approve</strong> in the
  Actions menu. Approving sends nothing to investors; notices go out only when someone clicks Send Notification.
  If you have any doubt about the figures, reply to <%= @actor&.full_name || "the person who asked" %> instead.</p>
<% when "approval_withdrawn" %>
  <p><strong>Why you got this:</strong> your firm requires a second person to approve capital calls and distributions
  (maker–checker). The figures changed after approval, so the approval no longer covers them and was withdrawn
  automatically. You are an approver or a preparer of this <%= noun %>.</p>
  <p><strong>What to do:</strong> an approver who did not change the figures should open the <%= noun %>, check the new
  figures and approve it again. If the change was not expected, ask <%= @actor&.full_name || "the person who made it" %>
  about it before approving.</p>
<% when "maker_checker_off" %>
  <p><strong>Why you got this:</strong> you are a company admin or an approver of <%= @entity.name %>. CapHive tells
  every admin and approver when the "second person approves" rule is switched off, so the control can't be removed
  quietly. While it is off, the person who prepared a capital call or distribution can approve it themselves.</p>
  <p><strong>If you expected this,</strong> there is nothing to do.<br>
  <strong>If you did not,</strong> a company admin can switch it back on in Settings › Entity › Edit › Approvals; the
  change is also recorded in the entity's audit trail.</p>
<% end %>

<% if @record %>
  <% path_url = @record.is_a?(CapitalCall) ? capital_call_url(@record, subdomain: @entity.sub_domain) : capital_distribution_url(@record, subdomain: @entity.sub_domain) %>
  <p><%= link_to "Open #{noun}", path_url, class: "btn btn-outline-primary" %></p>
<% end %>

<p>Thank you,<br><%= @entity.name %> System</p>
